[0.746, "o", "  Usage: pd watch <channel> --exec <script>\r\n  \r\n  Subscribes to a pub/sub channel and runs a script on each message.\r\n  Declared logical channels auto-resolve against the current repo/worktree by default.\r\n  Reconnects automatically with exponential backoff (1s → 2s → 4s … 30s).\r\n  \r\n  Options:\r\n    --exec <script>          Shell command to run on each message (required)\r\n    --once                   Exit after first message\r\n    --max-concurrent <n>     Max concurrent exec processes (default: 3)\r\n    --timeout <ms>           Per-exec timeout in ms (default: 30000)\r\n    --min-interval <ms>      Min ms between executions — rate limit (default: 0)\r\n    --dir <path>             Resolve declared logical channels for this worktree\r\n    --raw-channel            Bypass logical-channel resolution and use the literal string\r\n  \r\n  Environment variables set when exec runs:\r\n    PD_MESSAGE          Full message JSON string\r\n    PD_MESSAGE_CONTENT  Extracted content field\r\n"]
